From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: bind diagnose and expire netfilter flowtables

Add the PPE resource manager and rule translator used by netfilter
flowtable offload. A later patch publishes it through the PPE port
netdevices' ndo_setup_tc callback.

Expose compact flow identities, live hardware hit counters, active- flow
totals and CPU/drop reasons through read-only debugfs. Keep register
dependency snapshots out of the normal driver diagnostics.

Publish the already initialized PPE flowtable implementation through the
physical-port ndo_setup_tc callback. Keeping the flow-block binding in its
own patch makes this the explicit point at which the preceding resource and
translation code becomes reachable from netfilter.

Hardware-forwarded packets never revalidate their route in software, and
the per-flow hit counter counts at ingress lookup whether or not egress
delivery still works. A flow whose egress link went down would therefore
keep refreshing its conntrack timeout through the statistics reports while
black-holing every packet, wedged until the conntrack entry is removed by
hand: the software revalidation which tears down flows over a stale route
only runs on packets taking the software path, which a fully offloaded flow
never produces.

Merged from:
  0507-01-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-offload-netfilter-flowtables.patch
  0507-02-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-expose-flowtable-diagnostics.patch
  0507-03-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-bind-netfilter-flowtables.patch
  0507-04-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-expire-flows-of-link-down-ports.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

